Content shell: a permission the person has not decided reads as not decided.

patches/1023 made the shell deny what a browser would ask about. Its
status then read "denied" for every site before the site asked
(navigator.permissions.query(), Notification.permission), which no browser
shows: Chrome says "prompt" ("default") until the person answers, and
sites read a browser with everything refused in advance as an altered
one. The status is now
"prompt", and a request is still turned down, as a prompt the person
dismissed is: nothing is granted, and nothing is kept. Notifications stay
"denied", as Notification.permission says while there is no notification
service.

--- a/content/shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.cc
+++ b/content/shell/browser/shell_permission_manager.cc
@@ -145,9 +145,18 @@
     return blink::mojom::PermissionStatus::GRANTED;
   }
 
+  // zebkit: what the person has not decided reads as not decided ("prompt"),
+  // as in Chrome, not as refused: no browser shows a site every permission
+  // refused before it asked. A request is still turned down
+  // (RequestPermissionsFromCurrentDocument), as a prompt the person
+  // dismissed is, and nothing is kept. Notifications stay refused: there is
+  // no notification service to show them, and with none Chromium tells
+  // pages Notification.permission "denied", which the status agrees with.
+  if (permission_type == PermissionType::NOTIFICATIONS)
+    return blink::mojom::PermissionStatus::DENIED;
   return IsAllowlistedPermissionType(permission_type)
              ? blink::mojom::PermissionStatus::GRANTED
-             : blink::mojom::PermissionStatus::DENIED;
+             : blink::mojom::PermissionStatus::ASK;
 }
 
 PermissionResult
